@startuml 05-state-trade-lifecycle
title Trade lifecycle (row in PostgreSQL trades)

hide empty description

state "Not stored" as NotStored
state "Live\n(expired = N)" as Live
state "Expired\n(expired = Y)" as Expired

[*] -down-> NotStored
NotStored -down-> Live : [valid] submission\n/ ACCEPTED, createdDate = today
Live -down-> Expired : expiry job\n[maturityDate < today]\n/ EXPIRED
Expired -up[#green]-> Live : [valid, version >= stored]\nsubmission\n/ REPLACED, expired = N\n(A-09, A-19)

NotStored : rejected submission → REJECTED (audit only)
Live : valid submission, version >= stored → REPLACED, createdDate = today
Live : rejected submission → REJECTED, row unchanged
Expired : expiry job runs again → no change, no event (US-202.2)
Expired : rejected submission → REJECTED, row unchanged

note right of Expired
  Only a new valid version resets expired to N;
  the expiry job never does (US-204.2).
  Deletion and cancellation are out of scope (A-40),
  so there is no final state.
end note

@enduml
